15 0 obj
<< /Length 1184 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
72 720 Td
(.1. INT. DOWNTOWN CAIRO EDIT SUITE  -  NIGHT) '
(A narrow room above Talaat Harb Street. The city glows through dusty blinds. Two monitors hold the paused face of an elderly WITNESS.) '
(NOOR HADDAD, an independent documentary producer, watches the frame as if it might blink first. LAYLA MANSOUR, an editor with three coffees behind her, scrubs the timeline in FINAL CUT PRO.) '
(LAYLA) '
(Listen to the breath before the last sentence.) '
(She plays the clip. The Witness speaks with perfect sorrow. Too perfect.) '
(WITNESS \(ON SCREEN\)) '
(I saw the servers opened, and I saw every name inside.) '
(A tiny silence. No inhale. No movement in the throat.) '
(NOOR) '
(Again.) '
(Layla loops it. The room fills with the same manufactured grief.) '
(LAYLA) '
(The waveform repeats. Identical noise under different words.) '
(NOOR) '
(Witness Protocol premieres in Tribeca at eight. New York has seven hours.) '
(Noor checks the delivery card: WITNESS PROTOCOL  -  FINAL MASTER  -  APPROVED.) '
(LAYLA) '
(Approved by whom?) '
(NOOR) '
(Julian Voss.) '
(A message arrives from OWEN REED in New York: DO NOT SCREEN THE MASTER. CALL ME.) '
(> CUT TO:) '
ET
endstream
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /Length 1179 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
72 720 Td
(.2. INT. DOWNTOWN CAIRO EDIT SUITE  -  CONTINUOUS) '
(Layla opens the export metadata. Most fields are ordinary. One is not.) '
([[PROCESSOR: FACEFRAME 4.2 / DISTRIBUTOR: APPEL ONE]]) '
(LAYLA) '
(FaceFrame was not in our post pipeline.) '
(NOOR) '
(Neither was Appel One.) '
(A splash image appears: a silver fruit silhouette, one leaf tilted over the letter A. Beneath it: APPEL ONE  -  THINK BEYOND REAL.) '
(LAYLA) '
(That is close enough to Apple to be deliberate.) '
(Noor opens the delivery notes. They claim the sequence was optimized for VISION PRO presentation and finished with an authorized Apple workflow.) '
(NOOR) '
(We used Final Cut Pro. We did not use Vision Pro, and Apple never authorized this film.) '
(Layla finds FaceFrame edits on fourteen testimony shots.) '
(LAYLA) '
(The product did not clean the footage. It rebuilt the witness.) '
(Noor starts a secure screen recording, preserving the metadata without changing the source file.) '
(NOOR) '
(Copy the hashes. Do not open anything else until Owen joins.) '
(Outside, a car horn stretches into the night. Inside, the export clock continues counting toward New York.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /Length 1241 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
72 720 Td
(.3. INT. DOWNTOWN CAIRO EDIT SUITE / NEW YORK POST HOUSE  -  VIDEO CALL  -  NIGHT) '
(OWEN REED appears from a dark machine room in Manhattan. Behind him, a render farm blinks like a warning system.) '
(OWEN) '
(Julian moved the master through a private node. I copied the original witness plate before it vanished.) '
(NOOR) '
(Send the smallest verifiable fragment. Not the whole reel.) '
(A second window opens. JULIAN VOSS, immaculate in a studio office, joins without invitation.) '
(JULIAN) '
(You are delaying a premiere over compression artifacts.) '
(LAYLA) '
(Compression does not invent phonemes.) '
(JULIAN) '
(FaceFrame is restoration technology. Appel One cleared the workflow.) '
(NOOR) '
(Appel One is your company.) '
(Julian smiles as if ownership were a technicality.) '
(JULIAN) '
(It is a distribution partner.) '
(Owen sends a six-second source clip. The real Witness looks away from camera and whispers:) '
(WITNESS \(RECORDED\)) '
(??? ?????? ???????) '
(\(English translation: This image was fabricated.\)) '
(The sentence is absent from the delivered master.) '
(NOOR) '
(That is not restoration.) '
(JULIAN) '
(Careful, Noor. Names carry consequences.) '
(His window disappears.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
