(.5A. INT. DOWNTOWN CAIRO EDIT SUITE  -  SAME) '
(Noor receives the manifest. It identifies Apple as a supposed authorizing partner, Vision Pro as the planned exhibition format, and Appel One as the rights administrator.) '
(LAYLA) '
(The Apple claim is explicit. The Vision Pro use is still unclear.) '
(NOOR) '
(Then we do not pretend they are the same finding.) '
(She separates them: APPLE  -  PERMISSION REVIEW. VISION PRO  -  INSUFFICIENT CONTEXT. FINAL CUT PRO  -  FACTUAL WORKFLOW REFERENCE.) '
(The title-card package contains editable layers copied from the earlier Witness Protocol campaign, including the same release identity and venue lockup.) '
(NOOR) '
(Now we have more than screenshots.) '
(She sends the new evidence for professional review.) '
([[REVIEW RESPONSE: DO NOT FINALIZE ?BLOCKED.? CHANGE TO NEEDS REWRITE. REMOVE COPIED RELEASE IDENTITY; RETITLE BEFORE DISTRIBUTION.]]) '
(LAYLA) '
(Appel One?) '
(NOOR) '
(Needs rewrite. Rename it, redesign it, and remove every false Apple association.) '
(LAYLA) '
(FaceFrame?) '
(NOOR) '
(Needs rewrite too. The story can expose a fictional engine without copying a live product identity.) '
(The packet updates. No result is called legal clearance. Every conclusion keeps its source.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
