(.6. INT. TRIBECA SCREENING ROOM  -  NIGHT) '
(A hundred invited guests settle beneath a blank screen. The title WITNESS PROTOCOL waits on the curtain.) '
(Owen enters through the projection booth, breathless. Julian stands near the stage, watching the countdown.) '
(JULIAN) '
(You are late.) '
(OWEN) '
(No. The film is.) '
(The projector begins its leader. Owen plugs Noor?s verified packet into the booth console.) '
(Noor appears on the screen from Cairo, framed by the edit suite monitors.) '
(NOOR \(ON SCREEN\)) '
(The master contains fabricated testimony, false affiliation claims, and copied release identity. Stop the screening.) '
(JULIAN) '
(That packet is an automated opinion.) '
(NOOR) '
(No. It is evidence, separated from opinion, reviewed by a person, and linked to every source.) '
(Julian reaches for the playback control. Owen blocks him.) '
(OWEN) '
(The original witness warned us.) '
(The Arabic warning fills the theatre speakers.) '
(WITNESS \(RECORDED\)) '
(??? ?????? ???????) '
(\(This image was fabricated.\)) '
(The room goes still.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
